      "q": "1. What is the differen\nce between a polynomial and a rational expression?",
      "a": "wer\n: A polynomial is an algebraic expression involving sums and products of variables raised to non-negative integer powers with constant coefficients, whereas a rational expression is a ratio of two polynomials. A rational expression can involve division by a polynomial, whereas a polynomial cannot have division by a variable."
