      "a": "Here, sides of each of 10 triangular pieces of two different colours are\n$20\\;{\\text{cm}},50\\;{\\text{cm}}$\nand\n$50\\;{\\text{cm}}.$\nSemi-perimeter of each triangle\n$$(s) = \\dfrac{{20 + 50 + 50}}{2} = 60\\;{\\text{cm}}$$\nNow, Area of each triangle\n$ = \\sqrt {s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)} $\n$ = \\sqrt {60(60 - 20)(60 - 50)(60 - 50)} $\n$ = \\sqrt {60 \\times 40 \\times 10 \\times 10}\u00a0 = 200\\sqrt 6 \\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$\nAccording to question, there are 5 pieces of red colour and\n$$5$$\npieces of green colour.\nCloth required for\n$$5$$\nred pieces\n$ = 5 \\times 200\\sqrt 6\u00a0 = 1000\\sqrt 6 \\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$\nAnd Cloth required to\n$$5$$\ngreen pieces\n$ = 5 \\times 200\\sqrt 6\u00a0 = 1000\\sqrt 6 \\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$"
