      "q": "1. If the perimeter of one of the faces of a cube is $40\\;{\\text{cm}}$, them its volume is\n(a) $6000{{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}}$\n(b) $1600{{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}}$\n(c) $1000{{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}}$\n(d) $600{{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}}$29",
      "a": "(c)\n$1000{{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}}$\nThe perimeter of the one face of cube\n$ = 40\\;{\\text{cm}} = 4{\\text{a}}$\n${\\text{a}} = \\dfrac{{40\\;{\\text{cm}}}}{4} = 10\\;{\\text{cm}}$\nVolume of the cube is\n$$V = {a^3}$$\n${\\text{V}} = {\\text{a}} \\times {\\text{a}} \\times {\\text{a}}$\n$ = 10 \\times 10 \\times 10$\n$ = 1000\\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}$"
