      "a": "(b)\n$\\sqrt {abc} $\nLet length, width and height of cuboid be\n$$l,w$$\nand\n$h$\nrespectively\nConsidering adjacent faces: AEHD, DHGC and EFGH\nLet area of\n${\\text{AEHD}} = a$\n, area of\n${\\text{DHGC}} = {\\mathbf{b}}$\nand area of\n${\\text{EFGH}} = {\\mathbf{c}}$\nAlso, area of\n${\\text{AEHD}} = l{\\mathbf{w}}$\nArea of\n${\\text{DHGC}} = {\\mathbf{wh}}$\nArea of\n${\\text{EFGH}} = lh$\nTherefore,\n$lw = a,wh = b$\nand\n$lh = c$\n$ =\u00a0 > lw \\times wh \\times lh = a \\times b \\times c$\n$ =\u00a0 > {l^2}{w^2}{h^2} = abc$\n$ \\Rightarrow {(lwh)^2} = abc$\n$ =\u00a0 > {V^2} = abc$\n$ \\Rightarrow V = \\sqrt {abc} $\nVolume of cuboid is\n$V = \\sqrt {abc} $"
