      "a": "(ii)\n${V^2} = xyz$\nLet the 3 dimensions of the cuboid be\n${\\text{l}},{\\text{b}}$\nand\n${\\text{h}}$\nSo,\n$${\\text{x}} = {\\text{lb}}$$\n$${\\text{y}} = {\\text{bh}}$$\n$${\\text{z}} = {\\text{hl}}$$\nMultiplying above three equations,\n${\\text{xyz}} = {\\text{lb}} \\times {\\text{bh}} \\times {\\text{hl}}$\n$ = {1^2}{{\\mathbf{b}}^2}\\;{{\\text{h}}^2}$\nAs,\n$\n${\\text{V}} = {\\text{lbh}}$\n$\nSo,\n${{\\text{V}}^2} = {{\\text{l}}^2}\\;{{\\text{b}}^2}\\;{{\\text{h}}^2}\\;$\n${{\\text{V}}^2} = {\\text{xyz}}$"
