      "q": "16. A conical tent is $10\\;{\\text{m}}$ high and the radius of its base is $24\\;{\\text{m}}$ then slant height of the tent is\n(i) 26\n(ii) 27\n(iii) 28\n(iv) 29",
      "a": "(i) 26\nHeight\n$(h)$\nof conical tent\n$ = 10\\;{\\text{m}}$\nRadius\n$(r)$\nof conical tent\n$ = 24\\;{\\text{m}}$\nLet the slant height of the tent be\n$l$\n${l^2} = {h^2} + {r^2}$\n${l^2} = {(10)^2} + {(24)^2}$\n${l^2} = 100 + 576$\n${l^2} = 676$\n$l = \\sqrt {676} $\n$l = \\sqrt {{{26}^2}} $\n$l = 26\\;{\\text{m}}$\nTherefore, the slant height of the tent is\n$26\\;{\\text{m}}$\n."
