      "q": "17. Volume of hollow cylinder\n(i) $\\pi \\left( {{R^2} - {r^2}} \\right)h$\n(ii) $\\pi {R^2}h$\n(iii) $\\pi {r^2}h$\n(iv) $\\pi {r^2}\\left( {{h_1} - {h_2}} \\right)$",
      "a": "(i)\n$\\pi \\left( {{R^2} - {r^2}} \\right)h$\nThe formula to calculate the volume of a hollow cylinder is given as,\nVolume of hollow cylinder\n$ = \\pi \\left( {{{\\mathbf{R}}^2} - {{\\mathbf{r}}^2}} \\right){\\mathbf{h}}$\ncubic units,\nwhere, '\n$$R'$$\nis the outer radius, '\n$r$\n' is the inner radius, and, '\n$h$\n' is the height of the hollow cylinder."
