      "q": "18. Diameter of the base of a cone is $10.5\\;{\\text{cm}}$ and its slant height is $10\\;{\\text{cm}}$. then curved surface area.\n(i) $155\\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$\n(ii) $165\\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$\n(iii) $150\\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$\n(iv) none of these",
      "a": "(ii) $165\\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$\nDiameter of the base of the cone is\n$10.5\\;{\\text{cm}}$\nand slant height is\n$10\\;{\\text{cm}}$\n.\nCurved surface area of a right circular cone of base radius,\n$$'r'$$\nand slant height,\n$$l$$\nis\n$\\pi r$\n.\nDiameter,\n$d = 10.5\\;{\\text{cm}}$\nRadius,\n$r = 10.5/2\\;{\\text{cm}} = 5.25\\;{\\text{cm}}$\nSlant height,\n$l = 10\\;{\\text{cm}}$\nCurved surface area\n$ = \\pi {\\text{rl}}$\n$ = 3.14 \\times 5.25 \\times 10 = 165\\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$\nThus, curved surface area of the cone\n$ = 165\\;{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$\n."
