      "q": "21. A wooden bookshelf has external dimensions as follows: Height $ = 110\\;{\\text{cm}}$, Depth $$ = {\\text{ }}25$$cm, Breadth $ = 85\\;{\\text{cm}}$. The thickness of the planks is $5\\;{\\text{cm}}$ everywhere. The external faces are to be polished and the inner faces are to be painted. If the rate of polishing is $$20$$ paise per ${\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$ and the rate of painting is $$10$$ paise per ${\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}$, find the total expenses required for polishing and painting the surface of the bookshelf",
