      "a": "Inside diameter of the pipe\n$ = 24\\;{\\text{cm}}$\nOutside diameter of the pipe\n$ = 28\\;{\\text{cm}}$\nLength of the pipe\n$ = 35\\;{\\text{cm}} = {\\text{h}}$\nOutside radius of the pipe\n$ = \\dfrac{{28}}{2}\\;{\\text{cm}} = 14\\;{\\text{cm}} = R$${\\text{Volume}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{of}}{\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\text{the}}{\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\text{wood}}{\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\text{ = }}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{External}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{volume}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt}\u00a0 - {\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\text{Internal}}{\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\text{volume}}$\n$$ = \\pi {r^2}h - {\\pi ^2}l$$\n$ = \\pi\u00a0 \\times 35\\left( {{{14}^2} - {{12}^2}} \\right){\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\text{cu}}{\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\kern 1pt} {\\text{cm}}$\n$ = \\dfrac{{22}}{7} \\times 35(14 + 12)(14 - 12){\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{cu}}{\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\text{cm}}$\n$ = 5720{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{cu}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{cm}}$\nMass of\n$1{\\kern 1pt} \\,{\\kern 1pt} {\\text{cu}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{cm}} = 0.6\\;{\\text{g}}$\n$\\therefore $\nMass of the pipe\n$ = (0.6 \\times 5720)g$\n$ = 3432\\;{\\text{g}}$\n$ = 3.432\\;{\\text{kg}}$"
