      "a": "Depth of river\n$ = 3\\;{\\text{m}}$\nWater of the river\n$ = 40\\;{\\text{m}}$\nRate of flow of water\n$ = 2\\;{\\text{km}}/{\\text{hr}} = 2000\\;{\\text{m}}/{\\text{hr}}$\n$\\therefore $\nVolume of water flowing in one hour\n$ = 2000 \\times 40 \\times 3$\n$ = 240000{m^3}$\nHence, Volume of water flowing in one minute\n$ = \\dfrac{{240000}}{{60}} = 4000\\;{{\\text{m}}^3}$"
