      "a": "Let the missing frequencies be f\n1\nand f\n2\n.\n${x_i}$\n${f_i}$\n${f_i}{x_i}$\n0\n46\n0\n1\n${f_1}$\n${f_1}$\n2\n${f_2}$\n$2{f_2}$\n3\n25\n75\n4\n10\n40\n5\n5\n25\n$$\\sum {{f_i}}\u00a0 = 86 + {f_1} + {f_2}$$\n$$\\sum {{f_i}} {x_i} = 140 + {f_1} + 2{f_2}$$\nWe have:\n${\\text{N}} = 200$\n$\\therefore 200 = 86 + {f_1} + {f_2}$\n$114 = {f_1} + {f_2}.............({\\text{i}})$\nAlso, Mean\n$ = 1.46$\n$ \\Rightarrow 1.46 = \\dfrac{{\\sum {{f_i}} {x_i}}}{N}$\n$ \\Rightarrow 1.46 = \\dfrac{{140 + {f_1} + 2{f_2}}}{{200}}$\n$ \\Rightarrow 292 = 140 + {{\\text{f}}_1} + 2{{\\text{f}}_2}$\n$ \\Rightarrow 152 = {{\\text{f}}_1} + 2{{\\text{f}}_2}..........(ii)$\nSolving (i) and (ii), we get\n${{\\text{f}}_1} = 76$\nand\n${{\\text{f}}_2} = 38$"
