      "q": "11. Find the unknown entries (a, b, c, d, e, f) from the following frequency distribution of heights of 50 students in a class.\nClass Intervals (height in cm)\nFrequency\nCumulative Frequency\n150-155\n12\na\n155-160\nb\n25\n160-165\n10\nc\n165-170\nd\n43\n170-175\ne\n48\n175-180\n2\nf",
      "a": "Since the given frequency distribution is the frequency distribution of 50 students.\nTherefore,\n$g = 50$\nFrom the table, we have\n$a = 12,\\;\\;b + 12 = 25,\\;\\;12 + b + 10 = c,\\;\\;12 + b + 10 + d = 43$\n$12 + b + 10 + d + e = 48$\nand\n$12 + b + 10 + d + e + g = f$\nNow,\n${\\text{b}} + 12 = 25 \\Rightarrow {\\text{b}} = 13$\n$12 + b + 10 = c$\n$ \\Rightarrow 12 + 13 + 10 = {\\text{c}}$\n$ \\Rightarrow c = 35$\n$12 + b + 10 + d - 43$\n$ \\Rightarrow 12 + 13 + 10 + d = 43$\n$ \\Rightarrow d = 8$\n$12 + b + 10 + d + e = 48$\n$ \\Rightarrow 12 + 13 + 10 + 8 + e = 48$\n$ \\Rightarrow e = 5$\n$12 + b + 10 + d + e + 2 = f$\n$ \\Rightarrow 12 + 13 + 10 + 8 + 5 + 2 = f$\n$ \\Rightarrow \\;f = 50$\n5 Important Formulas from CBSE Class 9 Maths Chapter 12 Statistics\nS. No\nFormula\nDescription"
